DESIGN.md:315:   - **1030px, fourth pass (the one note that matters yields last).** Measured in headless Chromium against the in-memory fake at 1030px with two tabs, `Unread only`, preview and a sync failure: the status note clipped to `Sy…` (84 of 145px of words), the Preview tag to 88 of 124px, and the `Review access` link by 11px. Rule: at 1100px and below the trail yields in this order. (1) The Preview tag: its `· in-memory` detail goes first (`Preview`, 47px), then, while a visible account note or the read-only hint needs the room (`:has()` on the header), the whole tag drops to its accessible text and title; it is back above 1100px and whenever it is alone. (2) The read-only words collapse to the `Review access` link, which no longer shrinks (`flex-shrink: 0`). (3) The status note, last: it is a grid whose floor is its min-content, the lead (`Sync failed`, `Sign-in expired`) plus the link, because only the detail track (`· no network · 0 cached`) has a minimum of 0 and an ellipsis. The lead of a failure or an expired sign-in is `max-content` and never clips; neutral notes may ellipsize their lead. After: at 1030px the lead is 66px whole, the link 36px whole and the detail reads `· no netwo…`; `Review access` is 91px whole; tabs, `Inbox 18` (62px) and the chip (73px) are unchanged. jsdom cannot lay anything out, so `tests/layout/account-header-css.test.ts` pins the rules (the 1100px query, the `:has()` collapse, the grid columns, `min-width: min-content`, the detail ellipsis) and the opt-in rendered suite `tests/layout/account-header.rendered.test.ts` pins the result in real Chrome at 1030px (the tab strip does not overflow, the Inbox label keeps its full width, the `Sync failed` lead and the Retry link are whole) and the contact column leaving the grid with zero rows; the measurements above are from the first headless run.
